{
  "_comment": [
    "Canonical subject registry for the PYQ pipeline.",
    "Only entries under 'subjects' are loaded. Matching is exact, on whole words,",
    "longest alias first -- never fuzzy, because filenames contain typos",
    "('Futter.pdf') that a fuzzy matcher would confidently mis-resolve.",
    "",
    "Every expansion below is corroborated either by a real subject string already",
    "in the Neo4j faculty graph (FacultyMember.subjects_taught) or by the filename",
    "expanding its own abbreviation. Nothing here is guessed.",
    "",
    "'candidates' is IGNORED by the loader. It holds abbreviations seen in the",
    "corpus whose expansion could not be corroborated. Papers using them ingest",
    "with subject_status='unresolved' and still return a working Drive link.",
    "To adopt one: move it into 'subjects', give it a 'name', then re-run",
    "normalize + ingest -- the paper moves to its proper subject_key in place."
  ],
